Z||000000||84fierotrevor||11-12-2001||07:14 PM||||Well I just got back from Chris house.<BR>He is a awsome dude He gave me a free head for my fiero and a spoiler.<BR>Thanxs chris !<BR>But anyways i took it to my mechanic and he said it wont fit !!! I know it has to fit I looked at it myself. But he said look it doesnt have a water gasket hole ?<BR>IT'S OFF THE SAME DAMN FIERO !<BR>SO HE REFUSES TO STICK IT ON UNLESS THE CASTING NUMBERS MATCH ! and say 373.<BR>I am at his mercy now because My engine is in peaces at his place and i can't get it no where and I can't pay a tow truck to take it.<BR>What should I do ?<BR>He also said if he where to put it on the engine would overheat because it doesn't have that spot for the water to flow thru. and he is right because i compared the heads and my old one does have this other hole on it.<BR>any one know anything about this ??||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fierowrecker||11-12-2001||07:30 PM||||Hey Trevor!<BR>Is his name Earl or Lyle?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>The head will fit, and cool, just because the number does not match, does NOT mean it is the wrong head...<BR>I have 3 or 4 heads laying around, and they are pairs as far as the numbers go...<BR>But they are all compatible...<BR>And they are all off Fieros, just different years...<BR>In fact, my 86 has an 84 block with an 86 head, and it runs fine...<BR><P>------------------<BR>crash... The Fierowrecker<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/uploads/crash_sig.jpg">        <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif"> ||||reg||1
